WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.460
I want to do this next story today, because
it's important to do.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.430
But I want to be careful about the message
that I send to you.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.550
And I have something that I'm going to admit
to you, which is that Donald Trump's mishandling

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:17.720
of Corona virus has pushed me to be as close
to a prepper as I as as I have ever been.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:23.419
Now, preppers are those who believe that there
is a catastrophic disaster or emergency that

00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:25.880
is likely to occur in the future.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.849
And they make active preparations for it.

00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:30.619
Typically, they stockpile food.

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:33.060
Sometimes they stockpile weapons and ammunition.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.320
They stockpile elements of medical.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.280
As you may have come to know them and a whole
bunch of other supplies.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.500
And there's a political bent to prepping.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.530
So you've got just general people who in general
preparedness advocates who often are not super

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.760
politically entwined with the movement.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.800
But very often preppers are small government
conservatives.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.370
They're prepping because they have a fundamental
distrust of government.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:01.159
Sometimes they even have conspiracy theories
about government that lead them to prep.

00:01:01.159 --> 00:01:03.680
Sometimes you have religiously motivated prepping.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.479
Mormons, for example, often do long term food
storage as a part of their religion.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:11.480
Now, I am not literally becoming a prepper.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.890
I'm not buying guns, for example.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.950
I'm not buying a year of food or anything
like that.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:21.700
But there is no doubt that the degree to which
Donald Trump has been completely untrustworthy

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:27.009
and dishonest and incompetent day in and day
out when it comes to the Corona virus, a pandemic

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:31.700
has proven to me not that I need to have a
fundamental distrust of government and therefore

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.649
I should be prepping, but that the country
is dumb enough to elect people this poorly

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:37.340
suited to manage a crisis.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.540
And I do need to be more prepared.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:44.110
It's healthy to have a skepticism of government's
ability to solve every problem.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.420
And I've never trusted government in certain
areas.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:51.920
So, for example, I've never trusted government
